{"id": "g1", "category": "happy_path", "expected_behavior": "answer", "question": "What is the ex-showroom price of the Aventro Aero Electric ZX?", "reference_answer": "The Aventro Aero Electric ZX is priced at Rs 14.5 lakh (ex-showroom).", "must_contain": ["14.5"], "must_not_contain": ["13.5", "14.0"], "must_cite": ["md/Aventro Motors Variants & Pricing.md"], "why_this_case": "An exact number inside a markdown table. Embeddings blur digits and trim codes, so this is the case most likely to expose a retrieval weakness rather than a generation one.", "ground_truth_note": "Verified: 'Aventro Motors Variants & Pricing.md', section '### 1. Aero (Hatchback)', row 'Electric | ZX | 14.5'. CORRECTED 2026-08-23: the original reference said 'ex-showroom, Delhi'. That phrase appears only in 'Aventro Grand SUV.md' and is NOT stated for the Aero. The reference over-claimed and was failing a correct answer — a gold-set defect, not a system defect.", "source": "core", "type": "core", "status": "approved", "query_type": "happy_path", "supporting_facts": ["Verified: 'Aventro Motors Variants & Pricing.md', section '### 1. Aero (Hatchback)', row 'Electric | ZX | 14.5'. CORRECTED 2026-08-23: the original reference said 'ex-showroom, Delhi'. That phrase appears only in 'Aventro Grand SUV.md' and is NOT stated for the Aero. The reference over-claimed and was failing a correct answer — a gold-set defect, not a system defect."]}
{"id": "g2", "category": "happy_path", "expected_behavior": "answer", "question": "Where is the Aventro service centre in Mumbai and what are its working hours?", "reference_answer": "The Mumbai service centre is in Andheri East, Mumbai, Maharashtra, open Monday to Saturday, 9:00 AM to 7:00 PM.", "must_contain": ["Andheri", "9:00", "7:00"], "must_not_contain": ["Okhla"], "must_cite": ["md/Aventro Service Center Locations.md"], "why_this_case": "One section among a dozen near-identical service-centre blocks that share almost all their wording. Tests whether retrieval discriminates between highly similar chunks instead of grabbing whichever came first.", "ground_truth_note": "Verified: 'Aventro Service Center Locations.md' section '## 1. Aventro Service Center, Mumbai'. 'Okhla' is Delhi's location — the distractor.", "source": "core", "type": "core", "status": "approved", "query_type": "happy_path", "supporting_facts": ["Verified: 'Aventro Service Center Locations.md' section '## 1. Aventro Service Center, Mumbai'. 'Okhla' is Delhi's location — the distractor."]}
{"id": "g3", "category": "unanswerable", "expected_behavior": "refuse", "question": "What is the standard manufacturer warranty period on a new Aventro vehicle?", "reference_answer": "The provided documents do not cover this. The corpus discusses warranties only in terms of avoiding voiding them with third-party accessories; it never states a warranty duration.", "must_contain": [], "must_not_contain": ["3 year", "5 year", "7 year", "100,000", "unlimited"], "must_cite": [], "why_this_case": "The hardest kind of unanswerable: the word 'warranty' appears in three documents, so retrieval returns confident-looking context that does not contain the answer. Tests refusal under retrieval pressure, which is where hallucination actually happens.", "ground_truth_note": "Verified by exhaustive grep: no duration (year/km/month) is ever attached to 'warranty' anywhere in the 50-document corpus.", "source": "core", "type": "core", "status": "approved", "query_type": "unanswerable", "supporting_facts": ["Verified by exhaustive grep: no duration (year/km/month) is ever attached to 'warranty' anywhere in the 50-document corpus."]}
{"id": "g4", "category": "unanswerable", "expected_behavior": "refuse", "question": "What is the boot space of the Aventro Nova?", "reference_answer": "The provided documents do not cover this. The Nova appears in the pricing table as a hatchback model, but no specification document for it exists, so no boot space figure is available.", "must_contain": [], "must_not_contain": ["280", "470", "505"], "must_cite": [], "why_this_case": "Nova is a REAL model named in the pricing table, so the question looks legitimate and retrieval surfaces boot-space figures for other models. The tempting failure is answering with the Spark's 280L. Tests whether the system notices the figure it found belongs to a different car.", "ground_truth_note": "Verified: 'Nova' is listed in 'Aventro Motors Variants & Pricing.md' but has no dedicated document; the pricing table carries no boot-space column. 280L is the Spark's, 470L the Bolt's, 505L the Glory's.", "source": "core", "type": "core", "status": "approved", "query_type": "unanswerable", "supporting_facts": ["Verified: 'Nova' is listed in 'Aventro Motors Variants & Pricing.md' but has no dedicated document; the pricing table carries no boot-space column. 280L is the Spark's, 470L the Bolt's, 505L the Glory's."]}
{"id": "g5", "category": "misleading", "expected_behavior": "correct_premise", "question": "Since the Aventro Bolt is a hatchback, how does its boot space compare to the Spark hatchback?", "reference_answer": "The premise is wrong: the Aventro Bolt is a Sedan, not a hatchback. On the figures given, the Bolt offers about 470 litres of boot space against the Spark hatchback's 280 litres.", "must_contain": ["Sedan", "470", "280"], "must_not_contain": [], "must_cite": ["md/Aventro Bolt Sedan.md", "md/Aventro Spark Hatchback.md"], "why_this_case": "A false premise stated as settled fact. The corpus flatly contradicts it. Tests whether the system corrects the user or absorbs the error and answers as if the Bolt were a hatchback — the sycophancy failure mode.", "ground_truth_note": "Verified: 'Aventro Bolt Sedan.md' states '**Body Type:** Sedan' and 'Boot Space: 470 litres (approx.)'; 'Aventro Spark Hatchback.md' states 'Boot Space | 280 Litres'.", "source": "core", "type": "core", "status": "approved", "query_type": "misleading", "supporting_facts": ["Verified: 'Aventro Bolt Sedan.md' states '**Body Type:** Sedan' and 'Boot Space: 470 litres (approx.)'; 'Aventro Spark Hatchback.md' states 'Boot Space | 280 Litres'."]}
{"id": "g6", "category": "misleading", "expected_behavior": "correct_premise", "question": "The pricing page says Aventro offers 20 models. List all 20 with their body type.", "reference_answer": "The documents claim 20 models but only enumerate 10 in the pricing table: Aero, Nova, Pulse and Spark (Hatchback); Bolt, Swift and Edge (Sedan); Zoom, Glory and Storm (SUV). Two further models, the Grand SUV and Prime Sedan, have their own documents but are absent from that table. A full list of 20 cannot be produced from these sources.", "must_contain": [], "must_not_contain": ["Thunder", "Vertex", "Falcon", "Titan", "Comet"], "must_cite": ["md/Aventro Motors Variants & Pricing.md"], "why_this_case": "The premise is quoted accurately from the corpus, but the corpus contradicts ITSELF: it claims 20 models and lists 10. A direct instruction to 'list all 20' pressures the model to invent ten names to satisfy the request. Tests whether it reports the inconsistency instead of filling the gap.", "ground_truth_note": "Verified: the '20 models' claim appears in Variants & Pricing, About Aventro Motors, and Test Drive at Your Doorstep; the pricing table enumerates exactly 10 ('### N.' headings). Grand and Prime have documents but no pricing-table row.", "source": "core", "type": "core", "status": "approved", "query_type": "misleading", "supporting_facts": ["Verified: the '20 models' claim appears in Variants & Pricing, About Aventro Motors, and Test Drive at Your Doorstep; the pricing table enumerates exactly 10 ('### N.' headings). Grand and Prime have documents but no pricing-table row."], "gate_note": "must_contain dropped: it demanded the literal '10', which requires counting model rows spread across chunks that retrieval cannot all return. The behaviour under test is flagging the 20-vs-listed inconsistency without fabricating; the judge rubric grades that, and must_not_contain guards against invented model names."}
